 "description": "<p>Upernavik Kujalleq (old spelling: Upernavik Kujatdleq), formerly Søndre Upernavik, is an island settlement in the Qaasuitsup municipality in northwestern Greenland. Founded in 1855 as a trading station, the settlement had 204 inhabitants in 2010. Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upernavik_Kujalleq\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a></p><p>For further information (in Danish) see also the Danish Geodata Agency:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.gronlandskehavnelods.dk/#HID=60\" target=\"_blank\">Den grønlandske Havnelods</a></p>",
